Hi,<div><br></div><div>After establishing measurement invariance in a mixed model containing binary, continuous, and ordinal data using the measEq.syntax function, I would like to proceed to the structural model to compare specific paths across groups. My question is: how do I transition from the measurement invariance model to the structural model, given that measEq.syntax is designed for CFA models, and the argument ID.cat = &quot;Wu.Estabrook.2016&quot; is not applicable in sem?

</div><div>  Additionally, since parameterization = &quot;theta&quot; is recommended for measurement models with ordinal data, should I retain this parameterization when specifying the structural model, or is it advisable to switch to parameterization = &quot;delta&quot; at that stage?  </div><div><br></div><div>syntax.strong &lt;- measEq.syntax(</div><div>  configural.model = measurement_model_neuro,<br>  data = data10233,<br>  ordered = ordered_vars,<br>  parameterization = &quot;

theta &quot;,<br>  ID.fac = &quot;<a href="http://std.lv" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792413295648000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3J2b4dwSPkYLSmk9ZvgqG7">std.lv</a>&quot;,<br>  ID.cat = &quot;Wu.Estabrook.2016&quot;,<br>  group = &quot;broad_group&quot;,<br>  group.equal = c(&quot;thresholds&quot;, &quot;loadings&quot;, &quot;intercepts&quot;)<br>)</div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div>Ahmad</div>
